{"id":"leetcode-1356","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Sort Integers by The Number of 1 Bits","summary":"Given an integer array, sort the integers first by the count of 1's in their binary representation, then by their value if the count of 1's is the same.","statement":"Given an integer array, sort the integers first by the count of 1's in their binary representation, then by their value if the count of 1's is the same. Return the sorted array.","constraints":["Values are nonnegative and distinct.","Sort by set-bit count, then numerical value ascending."],"topics":["sorting","bit-manipulation"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"sort_by_one_bit_count","parameters":[{"name":"arr","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"list[int]","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def sort_by_one_bit_count(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def sort_by_one_bit_count(arr):\n return sorted(arr,key=lambda value:(value.bit_count(),value))\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def sort_by_one_bit_count(arr):\n return sorted(arr,key=lambda value:(-value.bit_count(),value))\n","def sort_by_one_bit_count(arr):\n return sorted(arr,key=lambda value:(value.bit_count(),-value))\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n log n)","target_space_complexity":"O(n)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Python integers expose their population count directly; it can also be computed by clearing low set bits.","Use a compound sort key (bit_count,value).","Return the sorted values.","Tuple comparison applies exactly the required primary and secondary order."],"editorial":"Tuple comparison applies exactly the required primary and secondary order.","tests":[{"id":"lc-1356-1","ar